    <p>Conversely, several high-volume 2024 topics are losing normalized share: COVID-19 (-28.1%), Neoplasms (-40.8%), and Autism Spectrum Disorder (-33.4%). This is consistent with the post-pandemic normalization of research portfolios and suggests funding agencies may be rebalancing away from COVID-19 toward chronic disease and mental health.</p>

