  <section id="open-access-patterns">
    <h2>Open Access Adoption & Journal Landscape</h2>
    <p>Overall, {oa_overall:.1f}% of abstracts in the dataset are flagged as open access (available via PubMed Central). The yearly trajectory shows a notable increase from 64.1% in 2024 to 74.1% in 2025, before dropping to 53.8% in the partial 2026 data. The 2025 figure is the most policy-relevant: it represents a completed year with a substantial sample ({yearly[2025]:,} records) and suggests that OA adoption is genuinely accelerating.</p>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="chart">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['oa_by_year']}" alt="OA rate by year">
      </div>
      <div class="chart">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['oa_by_country']}" alt="OA rate by country">
      </div>
